            {
                "entry_id": "57349e79-4460-3644-a582-9850c1cdc7a6",
                "word": "snark",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f23f6ff5-2adb-3f46-8939-40332bebb951",
                        "entry_id": "57349e79-4460-3644-a582-9850c1cdc7a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "an attitude or expression of mocking irreverence and sarcasm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "80c0899d-8c36-43c5-b0ac-33b2380d391d",
                                "sense_id": "f23f6ff5-2adb-3f46-8939-40332bebb951",
                                "text": "Brit-wit, in fact, could be seen as the precursor to the communicative style valorized on these beratement panels and on fan/rating communities, namely snark or snarkasm. Snark, a hybrid of “snide” and “remark,\" is a biting, casual verbal attack. Its subtle insult comprises a tone that acts as a weapon to cut its target down to size."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85dd96b7-bb33-4f1f-a654-7d4918ec0199",
                                "sense_id": "f23f6ff5-2adb-3f46-8939-40332bebb951",
                                "text": "Snark will get you any way it can, fore and aft, and to hell with consistency. In a media society, snark is an easy way of seeming smart. […] Snark doesn't create a new image, a new idea. It's parasitic, referential, insinuating."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea016d1e-1cad-4e35-b920-7a3316b3759c",
                                "sense_id": "f23f6ff5-2adb-3f46-8939-40332bebb951",
                                "text": "She liked his smile. There was neither snark nor megalomania in it, as characterized so many smiles these days."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "71a38fa4-6668-4bb8-9899-bad61cab3d5c",
                        "source_entry_id": "57349e79-4460-3644-a582-9850c1cdc7a6",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "f23f6ff5-2adb-3f46-8939-40332bebb951"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
                        "word": "sarcasm"
                    },
                    {
